GitHub Upload Instructions
The SIL GitHub Repository for your manuscript contains the following elements:
1.	Folders
a.	Code
Upload any .do files required for replication, or send to project administrator for upload.
b.	Data 
Do not upload large data files. You may store any small files which are required for the operation of a replication routine. Large data files should be hosted externally. 
c.	Figures
Optional, any you’d like visitors to the repository to have easy access to.
d.	Manuscript
Optional.
2.	GitIgnore Files
GitIgnores are handled by the project administrator. Authors do not need to alter these. They set to ignore any uploads which would exceed project size limits, usually data. 
3.	READMEs 
a.	README.md 
Authors do not need to update. 
b.	README-template.md
Authors will fill in with their project specific info, template copied below.
c.	README-replication.md
Authors will fill in with their replication package file info, template copied below. 
Once authors have completed the required replication package templates, please notify the SIL account administrator so that they can publish your repository on the SIL page.

